    "narrative": "As we enter the home stretch of the 2026 campaign, Ghost Ride the WHIP leans heavily into high-floor performers against soft rotations. Our top-rated start today is **Corbin Carroll** (71.81), who faces Freeland in a hitter-friendly environment. Despite the platoon disadvantage, his explosive speed and park factors make him a mandatory start in our pursuit of stolen base dominance. Close behind is **Seiya Suzuki** (69.93) and **Mickey Moniak** (67.27); the latter is a primary beneficiary of a positive platoon split against Soroka, with his efficiency bolstered significantly by park dynamics. **James Wood** (62.69) also demands attention, as his elite .410 xwOBA and high-leadoff placement mitigate the hurdle of facing Anderson, positioning him as a high-upside play for run production.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision today was benching **Isaac Paredes** (50.19). While his platoon advantage against Gilbert would normally warrant a spot, his raw projection fell short of the efficiency baseline established by **Cole Young** and **Brice Turang**. We are playing a cautious game; despite **Brice Turang** facing an elite arm in Wheeler (3.25 xERA), his stolen base utility is essential to our 5x5 strategy. We remain wary of **Vinnie Pasquantino** (55.91) and **Moises Ballesteros** (51.69), as both are hitting into unfavorable L/L matchups today. With **Tyler Soderstrom** sidelined on the IL, we have no margin for error, and we will keep **Griffin Conine** and **Travis Bazzana** safely on the bench to preserve our remaining game caps, as their sub-40 scores do not justify the roster burn this late in the season.",
